= Reichstag Fire

A few days ago, shortly after 9 p.m., the Reichstag building was reported as on fire when a Berlin fire station received an alarm call, and firefighters were dispatched. Despite their efforts, most of the building was gutted. By 11:30 p.m., the fire was put out. The firefighters and police inspected the ruins and found 20 bundles of flammable material (firelighters) unburned lying about.

The police conducted a thorough search inside the building and found Van der Lubbe, who was arrested. However many in the reichtag are considering passing the Reichtag Fire decree.


- @Signdecree: Sign the decree suspending civil rights.
- @convincepresident: Convince [+ president +] to sign our Decree
- @parlaimentary_passing: Try to get this through parlaiment to legitimize it.
  
@Signdecree
view_if: president == "Braun"
on-arrival: can_percecute_political_opponents = 1; dnvp_in_government = 0; workers_spd += 15; unemployed_spd += 15; rural_spd += 15; new_middle_spd += 15; old_middle_spd += 15; rural_spd += 15; catholics_spd += 15; new_middle_nsdap += 5; old_middle_nsdap += 5; rural_nsdap += 5; catholics_nsdap += 5; kpd_relation -= 7; z_relation -= 3; dvp_relation -= 3; ddp_relation -= 3; dnvp_relation -= 7; nsdap_relation += 3;

[+ president +] signed a decree enabling the arrest and imprisonment of political opponents without specific charges, the banning of opposition publications and meetings, and the expansion of central government authority over the German states. The DNVP and KPD of course oppose this decree. Meanwhile Wilhelm II condemned this decree as a "blatant violation of the rule of law". However the DDP, DVP and Zentrum stayed silent on the bill. We easily began shutting down opposing media and exoanding SPD propaganda press, while NSDAP press was allowed as they support our government.

@convincepresident
view_if: president != "Braun"
on-arrival: workers_spd += 5; unemployed_spd += 5; rural_spd += 5; new_middle_spd += 5; old_middle_spd += 5; rural_spd += 5; catholics_spd += 5; new_middle_nsdap += 5; old_middle_nsdap += 5; rural_nsdap += 5; catholics_nsdap += 5; kpd_relation -= 7; z_relation -= 3; dvp_relation -= 3; ddp_relation -= 3; dnvp_relation += 3; nsdap_relation += 3;
We convinced [+ president +] signed a decree enabling the arrest and imprisonment of political opponents without specific charges, the banning of opposition publications and meetings, and the expansion of central government authority over the German states. The KPD of course opposes this decree. Meanwhile Wilhelm II condemned this decree as a "blatant violation of the rule of law". However the DDP, DVP, DNVP and Zentrum stayed silent on the bill. We easily began shutting down opposing media and exoanding SPD propaganda press, while NSDAP press was allowed as they support our government.

@parlaimentary_passing
go-to: billfails if dnvp_in_government = 1; billsuccess if dnvp_in_government = 0;

@billfails
on-arrival: workers_spd -= 5; unemployed_spd -= 5; rural_spd -= 5; new_middle_spd -= 5; old_middle_spd -= 5; rural_spd -= 5; catholics_spd -= 5; new_middle_nsdap -= 25; old_middle_nsdap -= 25; rural_nsdap -= 25; catholics_nsdap -= 25; kpd_relation -= 7; z_relation -= 7; dvp_relation -= 7; ddp_relation -= 7; dnvp_relation -= 7; nsdap_relation += 3;

The DNVP managed to block this bill from passing, while the entire opposition would universally vote against the bill. This would manage to become a fiasco for the SPD, but the one hit the hardest was the NSDAP, which lost their entire anti-democratic voterbase.
  
@billsuccess
on-arrival: can_percecute_political_opponents = 1; dnvp_in_government = 0; workers_spd += 15; unemployed_spd += 15; rural_spd += 15; new_middle_spd += 15; old_middle_spd += 15; rural_spd += 15; catholics_spd += 15; new_middle_nsdap += 15; old_middle_nsdap += 15; rural_nsdap += 15; catholics_nsdap += 15; kpd_relation -= 7; z_relation -= 3; dvp_relation -= 3; ddp_relation -= 3; dnvp_relation -= 7; nsdap_relation += 3;

We manage to pass the bill, which would give power to the SPD-NSDAP coalition to prececute opposing voices. This is a major victory for both parties.
